# innerHTML escaping

This app renders views with `innerHTML` and template literals. See `@SECURITY-HTML.md`.

## Required

- Run **every** user-facing or persisted string through `escapeHtml()` before interpolating it into HTML: task `title`, `description`, `label`, `due`, `assigneeInitials`, and any `prompt()` input.
- Escape attribute values as well (quotes are replaced). Never drop an unescaped task field into `href`, `title`, `data-*`, or text nodes.
- Shell markup in `layout.ts` / `main.ts` must stay static. Route names are enum-checked; do not paste raw hash fragments or user strings into the shell.

## Current helper

Each page that interpolates user data defines a local `escapeHtml`. If you extract a shared helper, keep the same replacements (`&`, `<`, `>`, `"`) and use it everywhere those fields are rendered.

## Do not

- Interpolate unescaped strings into templates.
- Switch to `innerHTML` for values that can be set with `textContent` when you are not already in a template.
- Treat `task.id` as trusted if it can originate from storage or the URL without validation.
